<title>USA: Iowa editorial writer wins Pulitzer Prize.</title>
<headline>Iowa editorial writer wins Pulitzer Prize.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Gartner of The Daily Tribune in Ames, Iowa, won the Pulitzer Prize on Monday for editorial writing for &quot;his common sense editorials about issues deeply affecting the lives of people in his community.&quot;</p>
<p>The Pulitzer Prize for editorial cartooning was awarded to Walt Handelsman of The Times-Picayune of New Orleans. His cartoons are frequently reprinted in The New York Times, Newsweek, Time and USA Today.</p>
